sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: fleet maintenance redesign 2026-11-03 (each Node visit runs node:converge); R3c: no rollout records, Swamp run history is the record. docs/reference/gateway-recovery.md#fleet-rollout.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: orbit fleet:rollout
  %% kind: fleet.rollout
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Pick Nodes when no Node<br/>IDs are given
  %%> When:
  %%> - when the Gateway records a release `verified`: it queues one admission
  %%> - once a day at 03:05 Europe/Amsterdam, when the window of the other Nodes opens; the schedule only queues the admission
  %%> - when an operator runs `orbit fleet:rollout`
  %%> - always while `ORBIT_FLEET_ROLLOUT=true`, and only for a commit whose Gateway release is verified
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - the verified release admits the rollout, as `gateway:release:deploy` says; the deleted `fleet-maintenance` schedule did it each minute until 2026-11-06
  %%> - most releases land outside the window, so a daily pass at window open visits the Nodes they deferred
  %%> - the admission waits while another rollout runs; Nodes without CLI intent need no CLI release
  %%> - a Node with CLI intent waits for its CLI release; the admission keeps its one-minute retry after admitting other Nodes
  %%> Picks:
  %%> - a Node whose last visit for this commit did not converge it, a drifted Node, or a Node not visited yet
  %%> - at most once per 5 minutes per Node; the last visit is read from earlier rollout results
  %%> - no Node after a failed Node that still waits its 5 minutes
  %%> - in risk order: `app-dev`, then `ci-runner` `metrics` `analytics`, then `database` `websocket` `vpn` `router`, then `app-prod` `ingress`
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-fleet-rollout
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the commit, the agent pin and each picked Node; CLI intent only for Nodes that require it
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - no other rollout is running
  loop each Node, in risk order
    Note over SW: Wait for the Node's window<br/>gate
    %%> Why:
    %%> - `app-dev`-only Nodes go at any hour; others only 03:00–06:00 Europe/Amsterdam
    %%> - a closed window defers the Node to a later pass; it is not a failure
    opt Node carries CLI intent
      SW->>N: Publish the CLI<br/>cli · node-cli-install
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the Gateway uses the shared CLI eligibility rule; failed publication stops this Node
    end
    SW->>N: Publish the observer<br/>observer
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a Node without CLI intent skips the CLI child and publishes its observer independently
    %%> - the running digest and active unit prove the pinned observer
  end
  alt every Node converged or deferred
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Operation result lists each Node's outcome; the next pass reads it
  else a Node fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>NODE · error_code
    %%> Why stop:
    %%> - later Nodes are not visited, so one bad release breaks at most one Node
    Note over GW: Alert once<br/>rollout_halted
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause; the next pass (a verified release, the daily window pass or an operator) starts again at this Node
    %%> - retries raise no new alert for the same Node, commit and error
  end
